# Server configuration for local development. Copy this file to .env in the same folder:
# `make run` (Docker) and the servers started with uv both read it.
#
# Clients never send Marketplace credentials through it: the HTTP server gets each caller's token
# and endpoint from the X-MPT-Authorization and X-MPT-Endpoint headers, and an IDE that starts the
# stdio server passes MARKETPLACE_API_TOKEN in its env block. Everything here is optional; leave a
# value empty to turn its feature off, or uncomment a line to change its default.

# ----- Documentation tools and docs:// resources (GitBook) -----
# Server settings, shared by every client: set them here for the HTTP server, since clients only
# send the X-MPT-* headers. An IDE that starts the stdio server can pass them in its env block
# instead. Restart the server after changing them: the documentation loads at startup
# API token from https://app.gitbook.com/account/tokens
GITBOOK_API_KEY=
# Space ID, the part after /s/ in app.gitbook.com/o/<org>/s/<space_id>
GITBOOK_SPACE_ID=
# Public site of the documentation, to add a browser link to each page
GITBOOK_PUBLIC_URL=https://docs.platform.softwareone.com

# ----- Usage analytics (HTTP server) -----
# PostgreSQL URL. Not needed with `make run-analytics`, which starts a local database and
# passes its URL; set it only to use another database
# ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@host:5432/database

# ----- stdio server run by hand (`make run-stdio`) -----
# Token of the single tenant, idt:TKN-XXXX-XXXX:secret
# MARKETPLACE_API_TOKEN=
# MARKETPLACE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.platform.softwareone.com

# ----- Defaults you rarely change -----
# Debug logs, hot reload and the debug tools; compose turns it on unless set to false
# DEBUG=true
# Endpoint of the HTTP server for clients that send no X-MPT-Endpoint
# HTTP_DEFAULT_BASE_URL=https://api.platform.softwareone.com
# Interface of the HTTP server: 127.0.0.1 for local requests only, 0.0.0.0 for any
# HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# JWT verification: JWKS URL (taken from the token's iss claim when empty) and clock skew
# JWT_JWKS_URL=
# JWT_EXP_LEEWAY_SECONDS=120
# GitBook API, page index refresh and concurrent requests
# GITBOOK_API_BASE_URL=https://api.gitbook.com/v1
# GITBOOK_CACHE_REFRESH_HOURS=24
# GITBOOK_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=2
